    "result": "I implemented `plan_extraction` in `solution.py` following all seven rules in `spec.md`. I haven't run it or any tests, since shell access wasn't available.\n\n- **Validation:** it rejects an empty `dest` with `ValueError`. For each member it raises `UnsafePathError` on a NUL character, a leading `/` or `\\`, or a drive prefix. It also raises when a `..` would climb above the destination, or when the name is empty after normalisation.\n- **Normalisation:** it treats `\\` as a separator and drops empty and `.` segments. A `..` segment pops the previous one. Only an exact `..` counts, so `..a` and `a..` stay ordinary names.\n- **Directory entries:** names ending in `/` or `\\` are validated but left out of the result.\n- **Duplicates:** two file members that normalise to the same path, compared case-insensitively, raise `UnsafePathError`. Directory entries don't count toward this check.\n- **Output:** it returns `dest` (trailing `/` stripped) + `/` + the normalised path, in input order, so `\"/\"` as `dest` gives `\"/name\"`. Any unsafe member raises before anything is returned, so there is never a partial plan.",
